title: Radar Chart
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

A radar chart (spider chart) plots multiple quantitative variables on axes radiating from the same center, making it easy to compare multi-dimensional profiles. Use it for skill assessments, product comparisons, and performance reviews. ''New in Mermaid 11.'' Uses `radar-beta`.

---

!! Basic example

```
radar-beta
    axis Speed, Cost, Quality, Support, Features
    Product A: 4, 3, 5, 4, 3
    Product B: 3, 5, 3, 3, 5
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
radar-beta
    axis Speed, Cost, Quality, Support, Features
    Product A: 4, 3, 5, 4, 3
    Product B: 3, 5, 3, 3, 5
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: Engineering team skills assessment

This example compares the competency profiles of three engineers across six skill axes. Each series value count must exactly match the number of axes (6 each).

```
%%{init: {"radar": {"width": 500, "height": 500}}}%%
radar-beta
    title Engineering Team Skills
    accTitle: Team competency radar chart
    accDescr: Radar chart comparing skills of Alice, Bob and Carol across six axes

    %% ── Skill axes ──────────────────────────────────
    axis Backend, Frontend, DevOps, Testing, Architecture, Communication

    %% ── Team member profiles ─────────────────────────
    Alice: 5, 3, 4, 4, 3, 5
    Bob: 3, 5, 3, 5, 2, 4
    Carol: 4, 4, 5, 3, 5, 3
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
%%{init: {"radar": {"width": 500, "height": 500}}}%%
radar-beta
    title Engineering Team Skills
    accTitle: Team competency radar chart
    accDescr: Radar chart comparing skills of Alice, Bob and Carol across six axes

    %% ── Skill axes ──────────────────────────────────
    axis Backend, Frontend, DevOps, Testing, Architecture, Communication

    %% ── Team member profiles ─────────────────────────
    Alice: 5, 3, 4, 4, 3, 5
    Bob: 3, 5, 3, 5, 2, 4
    Carol: 4, 4, 5, 3, 5, 3
$$$

---

!! Syntax

```
%%{init: {"radar": {"width": 500, "height": 500}}}%%
radar-beta
    title [Chart title]
    axis Label1, Label2, Label3, Label4, Label5
    Series Name: value1, value2, value3, value4, value5
```

''axis'' defines the spoke labels — every data series must have exactly the same number of values as there are axes.

|!Key|!Description|
|`title`|Chart heading displayed above the diagram|
|`axis`|Comma-separated list of axis labels|
|`curve N`|Override a series to use a curved line (N = series index, 0-based)|

''Config keys:'' `width` and `height` control canvas size via `%%{init: {"radar": {...}}}%%`.

!! Tips

* The number of values in each series must exactly match the axis count — mismatches cause a parse error.
* `radar-beta` has a native built-in legend (enabled by default via `showLegend`); no WikiText legend table is needed.
* Scale values are typically 1–5 or 0–10 for readability.
* `radar-beta` is still beta — syntax may evolve in future Mermaid versions.

